<%- include("partials/header") %>

<style>
  body {
    background: #f3f4f6;
    font-family: "Inter", roboto, sans-serif;
  }
.guide-page {
  max-width: 900px;
  margin: 40px auto;
  padding: 20px;
}

.guide-card {
  background: #fff;
  border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
  border-radius: 12px;
  padding: 24px;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}
/* apply css to list items inside the guide-card */
  li {
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }


.guide-step {
 display: none; /* hide all steps by default */
}

.guide-step.active {
  display: block; /* only active step shows */
}

.guide-navigation {
  margin-top: 30px;
  padding-top: 20px;
  border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
}

.guide-refresh-warning {
  background: #fffbeb;
  border: 1px solid #f59e0b;
  color: #92400e;
  border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 12px 15px;
  margin-bottom: 15px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

.step-nav {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 12px;
}

.step-nav .btn {
  min-width: 120px;
  font-size: 15px;
  border-radius: 8px;
  background-color: #065f46;
  color: #fff;
  border: 1px solid #065f46;
  padding: 10px 16px;
}

.guide-step:last-child {
  border-bottom: none;
  margin-bottom: 0;
  padding-bottom: 0;
}

.guide-step h3 {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.guide-step p {
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  line-height: 1.6;
}

.guide-actions {
  margin-top: 10px;
}

.guide-actions .btn {
  margin-right: 10px;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------
   Deployment Guide Form Styling
--------------------------------------- */

.guide-step label {
  display: block;
  margin-top: 16px;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
  font-weight: 600;
}

.guide-step input {
  width: 100%;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  padding: 11px 12px;
  border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
  border-radius: 8px;
  font-size: 15px;
  background: #fff;
}

.guide-step input:focus {
  outline: none;
  border-color: #6366f1;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.12);
}

.guide-step input::placeholder {
  color: #9ca3af;
}

.env-field {
  margin-bottom: 16px;
}

.guide-note {
  background: #f8fafc;
  border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 12px 14px;
  margin-top: 15px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}

.code-box {
  background: #f8fafc;
  border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
  border-radius: 8px;
  padding: 12px;
  margin-top: 10px;
  font-family: monospace;
  word-break: break-all;
}

.success-banner {
  background: #ecfdf5;
  border: 1px solid #10b981;
  color: #065f46;
  border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 15px;
  margin-bottom: 20px;
}

.render-env-variable {
  border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
  border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 16px;
  margin-top: 16px;
  background: #f8fafc;
}

.render-env-variable h4 {
  margin-top: 0;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
}

.copy-field {
  display: flex;
  gap: 8px;
  margin-bottom: 14px;
}

.copy-field input {
  flex: 1;
  min-width: 0;
}

.copy-field .btn {
  white-space: nowrap;
}
</style>

<section class="guide-page">

  <h1><%= product.name %> Deployment Guide</h1>

  <div class="success-banner">
    ✅ Your template source code has been uploaded successfully.
    Follow the steps below to finish your deployment. read all steps carefully before proceeding. 
  </div>

  <div class="guide-step active">

    <h2>🗄️ Set Up Your Database</h2>

    <p>
      Your <strong><%= product.name %></strong> application
      requires MongoDB to store its data.
    </p>

    <p>
      Don't worry — we'll guide you through the setup step by step.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h3>Step 1: Create a MongoDB Account</h3>

    <p>
      If you already have a MongoDB account, simply sign in.
    </p>

    <p>
      For the fastest setup, choose
      <strong>Continue with Google</strong>
      and use your Google account.
    </p>



    <hr>

    <h3>Step 2: Skip the First-Time Setup</h3>

    <p>
      When you first sign in, MongoDB may ask questions
      about personalization or recommend additional setup.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can <strong>skip the personalization setup</strong>.
      You do not need to complete any additional setup.
    </p>

    <p>
      Continue until you reach the MongoDB dashboard.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h3>Step 3: Create Your Free Cluster</h3>

    <ol>
      <li>
        Click the <strong>3 line menu icon</strong> in the
        top-left corner.
      </li>

      <li>
        A side menu will open.
      </li>

      <li>
        Find and click <strong>Clusters</strong>.
      </li>

      <li>
        If you do not already have a cluster,
        MongoDB will ask you to create one.
      </li>

      <li>
        Select the <strong>Free</strong> plan.
      </li>

      <li>
        Click <strong>Create</strong>.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      Wait for MongoDB to finish creating your cluster.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h3>Step 4: Set Your Database Password</h3>

    <p>
      Open the MongoDB side menu again and go to:
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>Database & Network Access → Database Users</strong>
    </p>

    <p>
      Find the database user and click
      <strong>Edit</strong>.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>Click <strong>Edit Password</strong>.</li>
      <li>Enter a password you will remember.</li>
      <li>Save or update the user.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="success-banner">
      ⚠️ <strong>Important:</strong>
      Remember this password. You will need it in the next step.
    </div>

    <hr>

    <h3>Step 5: Allow Your Application to Connect</h3>

    <p>
      Stay inside <strong>Database & Network Access</strong>
      and click <strong>IP Access List</strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Click <strong>Add IP Address</strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
      For <strong>Access List Entry</strong>, enter:
    </p>

    <div class="code-box">
      0.0.0.0/0
    </div>

    <p>
      Leave the comment field empty and confirm the change.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h3>Step 6: Get Your MongoDB Connection String</h3>

    <p>
      Open the left menu and click <strong>Clusters</strong>.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>Find your cluster.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Connect</strong>.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>Drivers</strong>.</li>
      <li>
        Under <strong>Select your driver and version</strong>,
        choose <strong>Node.js</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Leave the driver version at its default value.
      </li>
      <li>
        Scroll down until you see the connection string.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      The connection string should begin with something similar to:
    </p>

    <div class="code-box">
      mongodb+srv://
    </div>

    <p>
      Click <strong>Copy</strong> and return to this page.
    </p>

    <div class="guide-actions">

      <a
        href="https://account.mongodb.com/account/register"
        target="_blank"
        class="btn primary"
      >
        Open MongoDB 
      </a> <br>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: #666;">
        come back and read over when you get stuck.
      </p>

    </div>

    <hr>

    <h3>Step 7: Enter Your MongoDB Details</h3>

  <p>
    Paste the connection string you copied from MongoDB
    exactly as it was provided.
  </p>

  <label for="mongoUri">
    <strong>MongoDB Connection String</strong>
  </label>

  <input
    type="text"
    id="mongoUri"
    name="mongoUri"
    placeholder="mongodb+srv://..."
    autocomplete="off"
  >

  <p>
    Example:
  </p>

  <div class="code-box">
    mongodb+srv://username:&lt;db_password&gt;@cluster0.example.mongodb.net/?appName=Cluster0
  </div>

  <hr>

  <label for="mongoPassword">
    <strong>MongoDB Password</strong>
  </label>

  <input
    type="password"
    id="mongoPassword"
    name="mongoPassword"
    placeholder="Enter the password you created in MongoDB"
    autocomplete="new-password"
  >

  <p>
    Enter the password you set for your MongoDB database user.
  </p>

  <hr>

  <label for="mongoDatabase">
    <strong>Database Name</strong>
  </label>

  <input
    type="text"
    id="mongoDatabase"
    name="mongoDatabase"
    value="<%= product.slug %>"
    placeholder="Enter your database name"
    autocomplete="off"
  >

  <p>
    This will be the database used by your
    <strong><%= product.name %></strong> application.
  </p>

  <div class="success-banner">
    🔐 Your MongoDB password is only used to build your
    connection string. Never share it publicly.
  </div>

  <button
    type="button"
    id="generateMongoUriBtn"
    class="btn primary"
  >
    Generate MongoDB Connection
  </button>

  <div
    id="mongoUriResult"
    style="display: none; margin-top: 20px;"
  >

    <label for="generatedMongoUri">
      <strong>✅ Your MONGO_URI is ready</strong>
    </label>

    <input
      type="text"
      id="generatedMongoUri"
      readonly
      autocomplete="off"
    >

    <div class="guide-actions">

      <button
        type="button"
        id="copyMongoUriBtn"
        class="btn"
      >
        📋 Copy MONGO_URI
      </button>

    </div>

    <div class="success-banner">
      ✅ Your MongoDB connection string has been generated.
      Keep it private and do not share it publicly.
    </div>

  </div>

  </div>

  <div class="guide-step">

    <h2>🔐 Configure Application Security</h2>

    <p>
      Your application needs secure secret keys.
      You don't need to create these yourself.
    </p>

    <p>
      We'll generate secure values for you automatically.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h3>JWT Secret</h3>

    <input
      type="text"
      id="jwtSecret"
      readonly
      autocomplete="off"
    >

    <button
      type="button"
      class="btn"
      id="generateJwtSecretBtn"
    >
      🔄 Generate Secret
    </button>

    <hr>

    <h3>Refresh Token Secret</h3>

    <input
      type="text"
      id="refreshTokenSecret"
      readonly
      autocomplete="off"
    >

    <button
      type="button"
      class="btn"
      id="generateRefreshSecretBtn"
    >
      🔄 Generate Secret
    </button>

    <div class="success-banner" style="margin-top: 20px;">
      🔒 These secrets are generated for your application.
      Keep them private.
    </div>

  </div>
  
  <% 
    const hasBrevo =
      envRequirements &&
      envRequirements.some(
        variable => variable.name === "BREVO_API_KEY"
      );
  %>
  <% if (hasBrevo) { %>
  <div class="guide-step">

    <h2>📧 Set Up Email with Brevo</h2>

    <p>
      <strong><%= product.name %></strong> uses Brevo
      to send emails from your application.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h3>Step 1: Open Brevo</h3>

    we will provide you with a link to open Brevo below. 
    Read the instructions carefully before proceeding.

    <h3>Step 2: Create Your API Key</h3>

    <ol>
      <li>Sign in to your Brevo account.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
      <li>Open <strong>SMTP & API</strong>.</li>
      <li>Select <strong>API Keys & MCP</strong>.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Generate a new API key</strong>.</li>
      <li>Give the key a name, such as <strong><%= product.name %></strong>.</li>
      <li>Generate the key.</li>
      <li>Copy the API key and keep it safe.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="success-banner">
      🔐 Keep your API key private. Do not share it with anyone.
    </div>

    <h3>Step 3: Add Your Sender Email</h3>

    <ol>
      <li>In Brevo, open <strong>Senders, Domains, IPs</strong>.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Add a sender</strong>.</li>
      <li>Enter the email address you want to use.</li>
      <li>Complete the verification using the code sent to your email.</li>
    </ol> <br>

    <div class="guide-actions">
      <a
        href="https://app.brevo.com/"
        target="_blank"
        class="btn primary"
      >
        Open Brevo
      </a><br>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: #666;">
        come back and read over when you get stuck.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3>Step 4: Enter Your Brevo Details</h3>

    <label for="BREVO_API_KEY">
      <strong>Brevo API Key</strong>
    </label>

    <input
      type="password"
      id="BREVO_API_KEY"
      name="BREVO_API_KEY"
      placeholder="Paste your Brevo API key"
      autocomplete="off"
    >

    <label for="EMAIL_SENDER">
      <strong>Sender Email</strong>
    </label>

    <input
      type="email"
      id="EMAIL_SENDER"
      name="EMAIL_SENDER"
      placeholder="you@example.com"
      autocomplete="email"
    >

    <p>
      Use the same email address that you verified in Brevo.
    </p>

  </div>
  <% } %>


  <%
    const hasStripe =
      envRequirements &&
      envRequirements.some(
        variable => variable.name === "STRIPE_SECRET_KEY"
      );
  %>

  <% if (hasStripe) { %>

  <div class="guide-step">

    <h2>💳 Set Up Stripe Payments</h2>

    <p>
      <strong><%= product.name %></strong> uses Stripe
      to process payments.
    </p>

    <hr>

    <h3>Step 1: Open Stripe</h3>
    <p> we will provide you with a link to open Stripe below.
       Read the instructions carefully before proceeding.</p>

    <h3>Step 2: Create Your Stripe Account</h3>

    <p>
      If you already have a Stripe account,
      sign in and continue.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>Choose <strong>Continue with Google</strong> if preferred.</li>
      <li>Complete your name and country.</li>
      <li>Enter your business information.</li>
      <li>Skip optional setup questions if available.</li>
      <li>Open <strong>Sandbox</strong> mode.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Step 3: Get Your Stripe API Keys</h3>

    <ol>
      <li>Click <strong>Developers</strong>.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>API keys</strong>.</li>
      <li>Copy your <strong>Publishable key</strong>.</li>
      <li>Copy your <strong>Secret key</strong>.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="guide-actions">
      <a
        href="https://dashboard.stripe.com/"
        target="_blank"
        class="btn primary"
      >
        Open Stripe
      </a> <br>
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: #666;">
        come back and read over when you get stuck.
      </p>
    </div>

    <label for="STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY">
      <strong>Publishable Key</strong>
    </label>

    <input
      type="text"
      id="STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY"
      name="STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY"
      placeholder="Paste your Stripe publishable key"
      autocomplete="off"
    >

    <label for="STRIPE_SECRET_KEY">
      <strong>Secret Key</strong>
    </label>

    <input
      type="password"
      id="STRIPE_SECRET_KEY"
      name="STRIPE_SECRET_KEY"
      placeholder="Paste your Stripe secret key"
      autocomplete="off"
    >

    <hr>

    <h3>Step 4: Create Your Stripe Webhook</h3>

    <p>
      Stripe needs a webhook so your application can receive
      successful checkout notifications.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>In Stripe, click <strong>Developers</strong>.</li>
      <li>Open <strong>Webhooks</strong>.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>Add endpoint</strong>.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>Webhook endpoint</strong>.</li>
      <li>Enter your webhook URL below.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="code-box">
      http://localhost:3000/api/payments/webhook
    </div>

    <p>
      If you are setting this up after deploying to Render,
      replace <strong>localhost:3000</strong> with your Render
      application URL.
    </p>

    <h3>Step 5: Select the Checkout Event</h3>

    <p>
      Your application needs the following Stripe event:
    </p>

    <div class="code-box">
      checkout.session.completed
    </div>

    <p>
      Select <strong>checkout.session.completed</strong>
      and continue.
    </p>

    <h3>Step 6: Get Your Webhook Secret</h3>

    <ol>
      <li>Create the webhook endpoint.</li>
      <li>Open the endpoint you created.</li>
      <li>Find the <strong>Signing secret</strong>.</li>
      <li>Click the eye icon.</li>
      <li>Copy the secret.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      Your webhook secret starts with <strong>whsec_</strong>.
    </p>

    <label for="STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET">
      <strong>Webhook Secret</strong>
    </label>

    <input
      type="password"
      id="STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET"
      name="STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET"
      placeholder="whsec_..."
      autocomplete="off"
    >

    <div class="success-banner">
      🔒 Keep your Stripe secret key and webhook secret private.
    </div>

  </div>

  <% } %>

